      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued October 31 at 3:28PM HST until November 2 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH AND WEST FACING SHORES OF NIIHAU\nKAUAI AND OAHU...\n...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH FACING SHORES OF MOLOKAI AND\nMAUI...\n\n.A moderate, long-period northwest (330 degrees) swell is expected\nto arrive this evening, and quickly build overnight. Advisory\nlevel surf is expected to Sunday for north and west facing\nshores exposed to the swell, with the swell expected to continue\ninto Monday. The swell may shift to a slightly more northerly\ndirection for a brief time Monday, before declining Tuesday.\n\n* WHAT...For north facing shores, building to 15 to 20 feet. For\nwest facing shores, building to 10 to 14 feet.\n\n* WHERE...North and west facing shores of Niihau, Kauai and Oahu,\nand north facing shores of Molokai and Maui.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 AM Sunday to 6 PM HST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
